---
title: "Render fixes: figure height, mermaid offline"
---

A small regression pin for two render/asset fixes (lane-d-render, 2026-06-27). Each
construct below exercises one fix. A third — a `{{< video >}}` source carrying a query
string, which had to stay positional rather than read as `key=value` — went with that
shortcode on 2026-08-08.

## A figure honoring both `width=` and `height=`

`height=` used to be silently dropped from the inline style; now it rides
alongside `width=`.

![A sized diagram.](diagram.png){#fig-sized width=320px height=240px}

## A mermaid diagram (offline-aware)

The diagram library is lazy-loaded from the vendored copy, so every build is already
offline; if it cannot load at all, the page shows a visible `[data-mermaid-error]` banner
instead of failing silently. `TALIESIN_MERMAID_URL` points the loader somewhere else.

```{mermaid}
%%| label: fig-flow
%%| fig-cap: "A tiny pipeline"
flowchart LR
  A[source] --> B[render] --> C[html]
```
